# EMPLACEMENT PARTS: thin pieces the baseshapes cannot make (a prefab's Scale is uniform). Four objects:
#   WatchRailX    - the Watch post's railing on its +X side (watchPost.pre's RailPX; turned 180 degrees: RailNX). The
#                   origin is the tower's top surface centre (y = 0 is the walk surface): a top rail 1 m up, a mid rail, a
#                   kick board along the floor and a post in the middle, along the edge between the corner posts.
#   WatchRailZ    - the same railing on the +Z side (RailPZ; turned 180 degrees: RailNZ).
#   BallistaShaft - the loaded bolt's shaft on the Ballista's stock (ballista.pre's Shaft): along -Z, 1.5 m long and
#                   8 cm thick, with two crossed fins at its back (+Z).
#   Arrow         - a guard's arrow in flight (arrow.pre): nose at -Z, 0.9 m long - a shaft, a flat head and two crossed
#                   fletchings at its back.
# Written by hand, like walkway.obj. Every piece is an axis-aligned box with flat facets: 8 positions a piece, the faces
# name them RELATIVE (-8 .. -1), and all pieces share one UV and these six normals: 1 +X  2 -X  3 +Y  4 -Y  5 +Z  6 -Z
vt 0.5 0.5
vn 1 0 0
vn -1 0 0
vn 0 1 0
vn 0 -1 0
vn 0 0 1
vn 0 0 -1

